{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775327700-1AgNsYSB94fbkMe2GxGN","role":"assistant","created":1775327704,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me start by understanding the task:\n\n1. I need to find when the Korean War started in terms of fiscal year\n2. Find appropriations for Federal Old-Age and Survivors Insurance trust fund for FY 1947\n3. Find appropriations for the same trust fund for the fiscal year when Korean War started\n4. Calculate CAGR (Compound Annual Growth Rate) in percent per year\n5. Round to nearest thousandth\n\nFirst, let me determine when the Korean War started. The Korean War started on June 25, 1950. The U.S. government fiscal year starts on October 1. So if the Korean War started in June 1950, it would be in FY 1950 (which runs from October 1, 1949 to September 30, 1950).\n\nNow let me look at the Treasury Bulletin documents to find the appropriations data.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_e0739bfabdfc92a9","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"ls -la /app/resources/"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
