{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775327704-trAklZgrFfmBPgHTNrSA","role":"assistant","created":1775327710,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The Korean War started on June 25, 1950, when North Korean forces crossed the 38th parallel into South Korea. The U.S. entered the war shortly after, and Congress declared war on June 30, 1950. For fiscal year purposes, the U.S. government fiscal year 1950 started on July 1, 1949 and ended on June 30, 1950. However, since the Korean War started in June 1950, it would be within FY1950 (July 1, 1949 - June 30, 1950), but the fighting continued into FY1951.\n\nActually, I need to be more careful here. Let me think about the fiscal years:\n- FY1947: July 1, 1946 - June 30, 1947\n- FY1948: July 1, 1947 - June 30, 1948\n- FY1949: July 1, 1948 - June 30, 1949\n- FY1950: July 1, 1949 - June 30, 1950\n\nThe Korean War started on June 25, 1950, which is in FY1950. So we're looking for appropriations from FY1947 to FY1950.\n\nNow I need to find the appropriations for the Federal Old-Age and Survivors Insurance trust fund. Let me search in the treasury bulletin documents.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_904cceaf09f2d4fa","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"rg -i \"Federal Old-Age and Survivors Insurance\" /app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1953_02.txt | head -20"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
